From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: fix FIT generator for out-of-tree (O=) builds

The FIT generator sources its helpers with "source ./${srctree}/...". When
building out-of-tree (make O=...), the Makefile exports ${srctree} as an
absolute path, so "./" + "/abs/path" becomes ".//abs/path", which is resolved
relative to the object tree and does not exist, breaking u-boot.its generation:

  make_fit_atf.sh: line 8: .//<srctree>/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh: No such file or directory

Drop the leading "./" so the absolute ${srctree} resolves correctly. In-tree
builds (${srctree}=".") are unaffected. fit_args.sh still resets srctree=$PWD
afterwards, so all later lookups stay in the object tree.

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
index 9639a06..dcf7509 100755
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 #
 
 # Process args and auto set variables
-source ./${srctree}/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_args.sh
+source ${srctree}/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_args.sh
 rm -f ${srctree}/*.digest ${srctree}/*.bin.gz ${srctree}/bl31_0x*.bin
 
 # Periph register
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/make_fit_atf.sh b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/make_fit_atf.sh
index 045273e..fa6a978 100755
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/make_fit_atf.sh
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/make_fit_atf.sh
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier:     GPL-2.0+
 #
 
-source ./${srctree}/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
+source ${srctree}/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
 
 gen_header
 gen_uboot_node
